### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Try the API without a frontend.
### In VS Code install the "REST Client" extension, then click
### "Send Request" above each block.
### Change @base to your Render URL to test production.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
@base = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Is the server alive?
GET {{base}}/api/health

### 2. Start a run - copy the runId from the response
POST {{base}}/api/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nickname": "Asha", "arena": "global" }

### 3. Answer "do nothing" (paste your runId)
POST {{base}}/api/answer
Content-Type: application/json

{ "runId": "PASTE_RUN_ID_HERE", "action": "none", "color": null, "reactionMs": null, "holdMs": null }

### 4. Try to cheat: claim a 5 ms reaction. The referee should say "invalid_timing".
POST {{base}}/api/answer
Content-Type: application/json

{ "runId": "PASTE_RUN_ID_HERE", "action": "click", "color": "red", "reactionMs": 5, "holdMs": null }

### 5. Leaderboard
GET {{base}}/api/leaderboard?limit=10&arena=global

### 6. Validation: a 1-letter nickname should return 422
POST {{base}}/api/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nickname": "x" }
